<Layout title="Sources & credits"><PageIntro eyebrow="A story with a record" title="Where the information comes from." description="The redesign combines the initial archival research with a later recovery of the original website’s non-blog pages, project map, media, and campaign directory." /><section class="section container article-grid"><div class="prose">
  <h2>The non-blog recovery.</h2><p>The original website became accessible again during the follow-up review on September 18, 2026. Its public WordPress API and sitemap exposed 65 pages, 28 posts, and 34 donation-form URLs. The 28 blog posts were explicitly excluded from transfer. The existing three editorial stories remain in place.</p><p>The site now includes {projects.length} project profiles, {history.length} project/prize history records, and {legacyPages.length} recovered resource, participation, and campaign pages. Recovered content is identified by its source and dates; a page’s modification date is not evidence that every activity it describes is current.</p>
  <ul><li><a href="https://abundantearthfoundation.org/wp-sitemap.xml">Original website sitemap</a></li><li><a href="https://abundantearthfoundation.org/projects-we-support/">Original project directory and annual lists</a></li><li><a href="https://abundantearthfoundation.org/">Original project map and partner marks</a></li><li><a href="https://abundantearthfoundation.org/donate/">Current published giving information</a></li><li><a href="https://abundantearthfoundation.org/our-team/">Published team biographies</a></li><li><a href="https://abundantearthfoundation.org/how-to-apply-for-funding/">Published funding-application status</a></li></ul>
  <h2>Original archival research.</h2><p>The first build drew on 2025 Wayback captures and a January 2022 funding page. Those sources remain attached to the existing editorial stories and historical profiles where relevant.</p><ul><li><a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250812100538/https://abundantearthfoundation.org/">Homepage, August 12, 2025</a></li><li><a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250520032712/https://abundantearthfoundation.org/projects-we-support/">Project directory, May 20, 2025</a></li><li><a href="https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/364631367">ProPublica’s IRS-derived nonprofit filings</a></li><li><a href="https://agroforestryrc.org/">Agroforestry Regeneration Communities</a></li><li><a href="https://www.eco-designers.com/">Eco-Designers</a></li></ul>
  <h2>Photography, maps, and identity.</h2><p>Recovered photographs, partner marks, and the original AEF logo remain the property of their rights holders. Source URLs and local copies are recorded in the repository’s migration manifest. Source captions are preserved where available; generic descriptions identify other images as coming from a project page.</p><p>The interactive history map uses coordinates from the original site, without inventing coordinates for records where they could not be recovered. Its base map uses public-domain Natural Earth data distributed through world-atlas. The searchable record list works independently of the map.</p><p>Fraunces and DM Sans are distributed under the SIL Open Font License. The redesign’s botanical mark, layout, and line graphics were created for this website.</p>
  <h2>Incomplete source records.</h2><p>Some original records have little more than a title. Some campaign pages and images could not be retrieved. Their verified identities or source references are retained, with no invented results. Payment history, private accounts, and a working replacement for the old form backend are not implied by this content recovery.</p>
</div><aside class="aside-card"><h2>Help improve the record.</h2><p>If you lead a project, hold image rights, or have more recent information, we welcome an update.</p><a class="button" href="/report-impact/">Share a project update</a></aside></section></Layout>
